targets.outcome_quote:
Our results also reinforce recent critiques that highlight the complexity of
using decision speed to infer dual systems (
Hutcherson et al., 2015
;
Krajbich et al.,
2015
). If manipulations of decision time induce strategic
choice adaptations, they may be less capable of informing some dual-system
models than previously believed (but see
Bago & De Neys, 2017
;
Pennycook et al.,
2016
). That is, time constraints may violate assumptions of
internal validity because they do not produce one single change in the
choice process (
Roberts
& Hutcherson, 2019
).
